WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.250
- [Narrator] We're told
a factory makes toys

00:02.250 --> 00:04.280
that are sold for $10 apiece.

00:04.280 --> 00:05.930
The factory has 40 workers,

00:05.930 --> 00:09.770
and they each produce 25 toys a day.

00:09.770 --> 00:13.320
The factory is open five days a week.

00:13.320 --> 00:15.007
What is the total value of toys

00:15.007 --> 00:17.570
the factory produces in a day?

00:17.570 --> 00:20.580
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:20.580 --> 00:22.860
All right, so let's
just think about a day,

00:22.860 --> 00:24.290
before I even look at this information.

00:24.290 --> 00:28.293
If I could figure out the value per toy,

00:29.780 --> 00:34.780
and then multiply that
times the number of toys,

00:34.900 --> 00:39.123
number of toys produced in a day,

00:43.290 --> 00:45.800
then we would have the total value.

00:45.800 --> 00:47.500
And let's see if they
give us that information.

00:47.500 --> 00:50.510
Well the value per toy,
they say the toys are sold

00:50.510 --> 00:53.910
for $10 apiece, so we
could write this this way.

00:53.910 --> 00:58.160
10 dollars per toy,

00:58.160 --> 01:00.130
and then they do tell us,

01:00.130 --> 01:02.500
or they give us the information
that we need to figure out

01:02.500 --> 01:04.110
how many are produced in a day.

01:04.110 --> 01:09.110
We have 40 workers, and they
each produce 25 toys a day.

01:09.410 --> 01:11.220
So the amount that's produced in a day,

01:11.220 --> 01:13.350
is going to be 40 workers

01:16.542 --> 01:19.990
times 25 toys per worker.

01:21.710 --> 01:25.300
Now I could say 25 toys
per worker per day,

01:25.300 --> 01:27.050
and that makes the units
a little complicated,

01:27.050 --> 01:29.790
or I could just realize
that this entire expression

01:29.790 --> 01:32.850
I'm creating is talking about one day.

01:32.850 --> 01:35.290
So the total number of
toys produced in a day

01:35.290 --> 01:37.720
is going to be the
product of these things.

01:37.720 --> 01:39.380
And we can say that the units work out,

01:39.380 --> 01:41.860
just to make sure that we're
getting in the right direction.

01:41.860 --> 01:43.730
A toy in the denominator cancels out

01:43.730 --> 01:46.310
with the toys in the numerator, workers,

01:46.310 --> 01:48.130
when you multiply it, this
would be in the numerator,

01:48.130 --> 01:49.120
this in the denominator.

01:49.120 --> 01:51.750
So workers, workers cancel out.

01:51.750 --> 01:56.750
And so I'm gonna be left with
10 times 40 times 25 dollars.

01:56.840 --> 01:59.700
And I do want it written in dollars.

01:59.700 --> 02:04.700
And so this is going to be
equal to 10 times 40 is 400,

02:06.140 --> 02:10.370
and then 400 times 25, let's
see, that's going to be

02:10.370 --> 02:14.530
4 times 25 times 100 so
that's 100 times 100,

02:14.530 --> 02:17.810
which is 10,000, and then the units

02:17.810 --> 02:19.803
we're left with is dollars.

02:20.980 --> 02:23.670
And now you might be
saying, wait, we didn't use

02:23.670 --> 02:26.250
all of the information and
that's true, we didn't use

02:26.250 --> 02:28.570
the fact that the factory
is open 5 days a week.

02:28.570 --> 02:30.600
We didn't need to use that information.

02:30.600 --> 02:32.340
That would have been useful if they said,

02:32.340 --> 02:33.677
what is the total value of toys

02:33.677 --> 02:36.390
the factory produces in a week.

02:36.390 --> 02:39.257
Then we would have said their
value per day is $10,000,

02:39.257 --> 02:42.310
and we could even write
it this way, per day,

02:42.310 --> 02:47.270
and then multiply that
times 5 days in a week,

02:47.270 --> 02:49.020
and that would have
given us the total value

02:49.020 --> 02:50.290
of the production in a week.

02:50.290 --> 02:51.480
But that's not what they're asking for,

02:51.480 --> 02:53.860
so we don't need that other information,

02:53.860 --> 02:55.440
and so we don't have to go to that step.

02:55.440 --> 02:57.870
And so this is really
just extra information,

02:57.870 --> 03:00.423
probably to distract you a bit.
